            <ArticleTitle>Late regression of Cypher in-stent restenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>341-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2010.12.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We encountered a case of late regression after sirolimus-eluting stent restenosis. We report this case with intravascular ultrasound imaging demonstrating an intraluminal echolucent tissue, which looks like a black hole.</AbstractText>
